.TH NOTE 1 note\-VERSION
.SH NAME
note \- a sticky note
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B note
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR id ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B note
opens a new empty note pinned to every tag. Text is saved to
.I ~/notes
as you type.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r
open every saved note that is not open now.
.TP
.B \-p
pick a saved note in dmenu by its first line and open it.
.TP
.BI \-o " id"
open the saved note
.IR id .
.SH KEYS
Insert mode is the default. Escape switches to a small vim normal mode.
Ctrl+Shift+d throws the note into
.IR ~/notes/.trash .
Ctrl+Shift+v pastes the clipboard.
Ctrl+Shift+y copies the whole note to the clipboard.
Yanking with yy or yw also copies to the clipboard.
Copied text stays on the clipboard after the note closes, until something else is copied.
Ctrl+Shift+c cycles the note through five theme colors.
Lines that start with Arabic or Hebrew read right to left.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NOTES_DIR
where notes are kept instead of
.IR ~/notes .
